page("portable-grill-packing-checklist","Portable Grill Packing Checklist","A complete packing checklist for portable charcoal grilling: grill kit, fire kit, food kit and cleanup kit.","both02",f"""
<h2>Grill kit</h2>{ul(["<a href='"+COMPACT+"'>Slot Grill</a> body, two grates and the two grate keys (they double as bottle openers)","Griddle plate(s), if you have the <a href='"+GRID+"'>griddle add-on</a>","Bag or box for the packed grill"])}
<h2>Fire kit</h2>{ul(["Chimney starter","Charcoal (sealed bin or bag) or dry cooking wood where allowed","Lighter, newspaper or natural starters","Heat-safe gloves"])}
<h2>Cooking kit</h2>{ul(["Long tongs and a spatula; scraper","<a href='"+THERMO+"'>Instant-read thermometer</a>","Separate trays for raw and cooked","Foil, oil, salt and pepper"])}
<h2>Food kit</h2>{ul(["Cooler, plenty of ice, raw meat sealed at the bottom","Prepped food labeled by cook order","Water, soap and paper towels for hands"])}
<h2>Cleanup kit</h2>{ul(["Lidded metal can for ash","Water or extinguisher","Trash bags","Oil or <a href='"+BALM+"'>Seasoning Balm</a> for the steel"])}
""","transport",[])

page("packing-a-grill-in-a-car-trunk","Packing a Portable Grill in a Car Trunk","How to fit a flat-pack charcoal grill, charcoal and cooler into a car trunk without soot, smells or rattles.","c07",f"""
<p>A flat pack is the friendliest grill shape for a car: it stands against the trunk wall or lies under the cooler.</p>
{table(["Model","Packed","Weight, grill only"],[["Compact","About 1&quot; thick","About 14 lb"],["Full Size","About 1.25&quot; thick","About 27.6 lb"]])}
<h2>Tips</h2>{ul(["Bag it: an old duffel or canvas bag keeps soot off upholstery.","Charcoal in a lidded bin keeps dust and smell contained.","Pack the cooler last so it's first out.","Never load a warm grill or ash. Wait until it's completely cold."])}
""","transport",[])

page("carrying-a-grill-on-a-kayak-canoe-or-backpack","Carrying a Portable Grill by Kayak, Canoe or on Foot","Weight and size considerations for carrying a flat-pack grill farther from the car: paddle trips and short walks to a picnic spot.","c13",f"""
<p>The Slot Grill Compact packs to about 1&quot; and weighs about 14 lb (grill only), according to SlotGrill.com, which makes it reasonable for a kayak or canoe trip or a short walk from the car. It is heavy steel, so it's not an ultralight backpacking grill.</p>
<h2>Paddling</h2>{ul(["Pack in a dry bag with charcoal in a separate waterproof bag.","Lay it flat at the bottom of the hull for stability.","Cook on shore only."])}
<h2>Walking in</h2>{ul(["Grill flat against your back in a pack; charcoal in a separate bag.","Bring only the charcoal you'll use."])}
""","transport",[])

page("storing-a-portable-grill-at-home","Storing a Portable Grill at Home","Where and how to store a carbon steel flat-pack grill between trips so it doesn't rust or make a mess.","both16",f"""
{ol(["Cool and empty the ash.","Scrape the grates; wipe cooking surfaces with a thin coat of oil.","Pack flat and bag it.","Store somewhere dry: a closet, under a bed, a garage shelf off the concrete.","Check it before the season; touch up rust with steel wool and oil."])}
<p>Slot Grill's FAQ says light surface rust is purely cosmetic: clean it off and re-season.</p>
""","transport",[])

page("cleaning-a-portable-grill-on-the-road","Cleaning a Portable Grill on the Road","How to clean a carbon steel grill at the campsite, beach or tailgate with minimal water, and finish properly at home.","c08",f"""
<h2>At the site</h2>{ol(["Scrape the grates while warm with a scraper or balled foil in tongs.","Scrape griddle plates; wipe with paper towels.","Let it cool completely; empty ash per site rules.","Wipe a thin coat of oil on cooking surfaces.","Bag it."])}
<h2>At home</h2>{ul(["Wash off salt or sand with water, dry right away (warm it over a few coals or in a warm oven if parts fit).","Re-oil.","Re-season if needed; see {0}.".format(L("seasoning-a-portable-grill-before-the-first-trip","seasoning"))])}
""","transport",[])

page("griddle-plates-on-the-go","Griddle Plates on the Go","How the Slot Grill griddle plates travel and what they add to portable cooking: breakfast, smash burgers and small foods.","grid1",f"""
<p>The <a href="{GRID}">Slot Grill Griddle Add-On</a> is a carbon steel flat-top plate for the grill's two-piece top: one plate and one grate, or two plates. Slot Grill says the plates stack with the grill so the whole setup still travels as one flat package.</p>
{table(["Model","Weight with 1 griddle","With 2 griddles"],[["Compact","16.2 lb","18.4 lb"],["Full Size","31.8 lb","36.4 lb"]])}
<h2>Why bring it</h2>{ul(["Breakfast: eggs, bacon, pancakes","Smash burgers","Quesadillas and grilled cheese","Shrimp and chopped veggies that fall through grates"])}
""","transport",[])
